{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgApohsmkKSJrF1PTt4c8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found the cause and fixed it in `site/robots.txt`. The full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** On 2026-09-07, `Disallow: /v1/` was added to `robots.txt`. Every note page is an empty HTML shell, and `app.js` fills it with data from `/v1/notes/{slug}`. Google follows `robots.txt` when it renders a page, so it wasn't allowed to fetch the note. The fetch failed, and `app.js` then showed its \"NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address\" screen with HTTP 200. Google treats a \"not found\" page served with HTTP 200 as a Soft 404.\n\nThe URL Inspection export shows exactly this: the page fetch succeeded, but the rendered text is the not-found screen. The dates match too: notes Google last crawled before Sep 7 are still indexed, and every one crawled after is a Soft 404. Browsers and curl ignore `robots.txt`, which is why the pages open fine for you.\n\n**Fix:** I only changed `robots.txt`:\n- It now allows the two public read endpoints the pages need: the note list (`/v1/notes?limit=50`) and single notes (`/v1/notes/{slug}`).\n- `/v1/notes/*/reactions` is blocked again with a longer rule. Google applies the most specific matching rule, so this wins over the allow.\n- `Disallow: /v1/` still covers `/v1/me`, the drafts and the sign-in endpoint, and `/admin/` stays blocked.\n\n**Check:** I tested 13 paths with a short script that applies rules the way Google does (longest match wins, `Allow` wins a tie). All 13 pass. Run against the old file, the same script shows the public read endpoints blocked, which confirms the cause.\n\nNothing was deployed and nothing was sent to Search Console. After you deploy, `ANSWER.md` lists the next steps:\n- check the live `robots.txt` (CloudFront may serve a cached copy until you clear it)\n- ask Search Console to recrawl `robots.txt`\n- run a live test on `/n/drip-line-pressure`, then request indexing for the affected pages (about 10 a day)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1646,"cache_read_input_tokens":25898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1646},"output_tokens":732,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83d0fd50-9592-4f02-9f10-fb1257f11f36","uuid":"de07a974-9421-4e38-a5c9-333736c15250","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:42:15.642Z","request_id":"req_011CgApohWSZUTnzUAfum2wr"}
